      "obligation": "refuter:3:1",
      "id": "ex-ag-differentials-polynomial-and-hypersurface",
      "location": "Example, final sentence",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The sentence says that when 2≠0 and 3≠0, “the quotient would be free of rank one.” But the preceding computation gives the cotangent fibre at the origin as Ω_A⊗_A k ≅ k². A free rank-one A-module has a one-dimensional fibre there, so the asserted freeness does not follow and is false.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "7df98873e27e525db21a76e571b7f63f4458c88b0317edd58af7cf169b5e24da"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:2",
      "id": "ex-ag-separable-and-inseparable-field-differentials",
      "location": "Title",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The title says “Separable extensions have no differentials and inseparable ones do.” Without an algebraic or finite-extension restriction this is false: for k=Fp(t) and L=union_n Fp(t^(1/p^n)), L/k is purely inseparable, but every element of L has a pth root in L, so Ω_{L/k}=0.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "f4c09188c2d972520e1cfa868d7c738296c9741e6072ba8c1dbd305d2f4b3c51"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:3",
      "id": "ex-ag-field-change-inseparable-thickening",
      "location": "Example, final sentence",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The sentence calls α “the point” of Spec k in the fibre of Spec L→Spec k. Here α is an element of L, not a point of Spec k; Spec k has only its unique point, whose fibre is Spec L. Spec(L⊗_k L) is instead the fibre product obtained by pulling Spec L back along Spec L→Spec k.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "1f400cf2171a52057cef806a2d85c45ddb4628635564ac2809636b125d03ff16"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:4",
      "id": "cex-ag-regular-factors-product-not-regular",
      "location": "Statement refuted",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The statement concerns R⊗_Z S, while the witness computes L⊗_k L and uses a⊗1=1⊗a for a∈k. That equality is imposed in a tensor product over k, not over Z, so the displayed nilpotent witness does not establish the stated claim about R⊗_Z S.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "52a7d9b077e102974fa3ca216dd397c43d420fa6715d02512047acae43220aa5"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:5",
      "id": "lem-ag-geometrically-regular-fibres-local-presentation",
      "location": "Facts [F11]",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "[F11] states that a module M has M_q=0 exactly when some g∉q annihilates M, with no finite-generation hypothesis. For R=Q[t], q=(0), and M=⊕_{a∈Q}R/(t−a), one has M_q=0, but no nonzero g∈R annihilates M: such a g would have to vanish at every rational a. Finite generation is needed for the claimed uniform annihilator.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "deb41665465cc0d73dab4b5df93891a2f95233ea88c3f320eeb97354d8639099"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:6",
      "id": "thm-ag-field-differentials-separable-rank",
      "location": "Proof step 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step calls D_j:K→K a “K′-linear derivation” extending ∂_j on K′. A K′-linear derivation must vanish on K′, whereas ∂_j(t_i)=δ_ij is nonzero for the relevant i. The construction can provide the needed k-derivation, but the stated linearity does not license the extension.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "9d18978b8de54e20f3da1edf15cc498cffe7253cfdc294d3207d7f87f276c82f"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:7",
      "id": "thm-ag-field-differentials-separable-rank",
      "location": "Proof step 5.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step says that prescribing b↦0 on K[B0] defines a “K-derivation” extending D:K→L. A K-derivation vanishes on K, so it cannot extend a nonzero k-derivation D on K. The argument is repairable by constructing a k-derivation extending D and killing B0.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "9d18978b8de54e20f3da1edf15cc498cffe7253cfdc294d3207d7f87f276c82f"
